{"text":"Now, don't get me wrong, I'm not saying people in the emerging markets don't understand democracy. Nor am I saying that they wouldn't ideally like to pick their presidents or their leaders. Of course they would. However, I am saying that on balance, they worry more about where their living standard improvements are going to come from and how it is that governments can deliver for them than whether or not the government was elected by democracy. The fact of the matter is that this has become a very poignant question because there is, for the first time in a long time, a real challenge to the Western ideological systems of politics and economics. And this is a system that is embodied by China. And rather than have private capitalism, they have state capitalism. Instead of liberal democracy, they have de-prioritized the democratic system. And they have also decided to prioritize economic rights over political rights.","words":[{"text":"Now","start":0.0,"end":0.72,"punct":","},{"text":"don't","start":0.74,"end":1.1},{"text":"get","start":1.1,"end":1.24},{"text":"me","start":1.24,"end":1.42},{"text":"wrong","start":1.42,"end":1.62,"punct":","},{"text":"I'm","start":1.76,"end":1.82},{"text":"not","start":1.82,"end":1.94},{"text":"saying","start":1.94,"end":2.18},{"text":"people","start":2.18,"end":2.4},{"text":"in","start":2.4,"end":2.54},{"text":"the","start":2.54,"end":2.62},{"text":"emerging","start":2.62,"end":2.86},{"text":"markets","start":2.86,"end":3.14},{"text":"don't","start":3.14,"end":3.4},{"text":"understand","start":3.4,"end":3.84},{"text":"democracy","start":3.84,"end":4.48,"punct":"."},{"text":"Nor","start":5.12,"end":5.46},{"text":"am","start":5.46,"end":5.68},{"text":"I","start":5.68,"end":5.84},{"text":"saying","start":5.84,"end":6.1},{"text":"that","start":6.1,"end":6.26},{"text":"they","start":6.26,"end":6.42},{"text":"wouldn't","start":6.42,"end":6.74},{"text":"ideally","start":6.74,"end":7.14},{"text":"like","start":7.14,"end":7.46},{"text"